/ event-action: what an event runs is an action. This goal is the plan's index and its proof: each comment a
/ behaviour, the test under it proves it. The text is start.md.
Start
- call Stage1
- call Stage2
- call Stage3
- call Stage4
- call BoyScout

Stage1
/ on.event answers the event's action, and on.unbind with Action=%action% takes it off; after, the event no longer
/ runs it — plang test
/ /plan/event-action/module/on/UnbindTakesTheAction
- call /plan/event-action/module/on/UnbindTakesTheAction
/ the surface golden and the decider fixtures are re-pinned under this decision — C# (SurfaceGolden, PickListTests,
/ ModulePageTests)

Stage2
/ "before each goal, call Log" binds through %!app.event.goal.start% and Log runs before each goal — plang test
/ /plan/event-action/app/event/BeforeEachGoal
- call /plan/event-action/app/event/BeforeEachGoal
/ %!app.event.goal.before% holds no action before the bind and one after — plang test
/ /plan/event-action/app/event/ReadTheBeforeSide
- call /plan/event-action/app/event/ReadTheBeforeSide
/ an action on %!app.event.goal["/Process"].start% runs for Process only, never for another goal — plang test
/ /plan/event-action/app/event/OneGoalsStart
- call /plan/event-action/app/event/OneGoalsStart
/ "after each file.read, call Audit" runs Audit after a file read — plang test
/ /plan/event-action/app/event/AfterEachFileRead
- call /plan/event-action/app/event/AfterEachFileRead
/ reading %!app.event.goal.before% in an app that bound nothing leaves %!app.event% empty — C#

Stage3
/ an action bound with Sub=none doesn't run in a sub app born after it; one bound without Sub does — plang test
/ /plan/event-action/app/event/SubNoneStaysHome
- call /plan/event-action/app/event/SubNoneStaysHome
/ a snapshot keeps an action's Sub, and a resumed app's sub app honours it — C#

Stage4
/ the debug watch, the test runner's timing, coverage and a mock each still run, and none is in a snapshot — C#
/ every core event but error is the event class, and a type's declared event ([Events("closed")]) binds and runs — C#

BoyScout
/ after on.unbind takes the last action off an item's events, %!app.event% no longer lists that item — C#
/ two actions made by one on.event step both run after a resume — C#
